    "summary": "Jazz‑rich second set with soaring horns and Keith’s killer solo",
    "blurb": "The Providence show shines on a horn‑driven second set that erupts after Truckin'. Eyes Of The World, Let It Grow and the Weather Report Suite are highlights, while Keith Godchaux delivers a standout solo on Let Me Sing Your Blues Away. Recording quality is excellent for the board‑sourced second half.",
    "review": "September 15, 1973 at the Providence Civic Center captures the Dead in a rare, jazz‑inflected mood. After a solid first set of rootsy classics, the band launches into a soaring second set that feels like a brass‑colored improv lab. The horn section lifts Mississippi Half‑Step Uptown Toodeloo into an energetic launchpad, and the subsequent jam on Eyes Of The World stretches into free‑form territory before segueing into Keith Godchaux’s soulful vocal lead and blistering solo on Let Me Sing Your Blues Away. The Weather Report Suite unfolds in two parts, feeding seamlessly into a glorious Let It Grow that showcases the group's telepathic interplay. The set closes with heartfelt renditions of Stella Blue and Sugar Magnolia, rounding out one of the season’s most memorable evenings. The soundboard recording (gd1973-09-15.sbd-set2.levy.01077.sbeok.shnf) preserves every nuance – from Jerry’s “blow‑me‑away” vocals to Bill Kreutzmann’s steady pulse – making this a must‑listen for fans of the band’s 1973 jazz explorations.",
